With the synthesized photocatalyst at room temperature, the absorbance (A) was measured using a UV–Vis Spectrophotometer (analytic Jena, Specord 200 plus) that scanned from 190 to 1100 nm. The normal protocol was followed in the preparation of the samples by dispersing Nanopowder in DW using an ultrasonicator and putting in a 1 cm quartz covet. To study the bandgap of the photocatalyst NPs, UV–Vis spectroscopic analyses were approved. The purpose of this study was to investigate the effect of extract types on the optical band gap (Eg) of synthesized samples. The following Eq. (1) was used to calculate Eg39:1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
